## A doc comment is trivia carried on the token below it, not a token of its
## own, so the formatter has to keep it above the same declaration and not
## merely somewhere near it.
##
## The formatter has no opinion about what is inside one: a `##` run is an
## ordinary comment to it, and `format_source` compares the doc run on every
## token before and after to make sure moving one is impossible.
type Doc:
    ## Attached to a field.
    title: String

    body: String

## Attached to a function, with a blank line between the run and the
## declaration, which the lexer does not mind.

def summarize(doc: borrowed Doc) -> String:
    doc.title

# An ordinary comment is not a doc run, however many hashes follow it on the
# same line: ### only documents when it starts the comment.
def plain() -> Int:
    1
